1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,379
Before a Zone business releases a withdrawal batch, a settlement counterparty may need to check it.

2
00:00:07,429 --> 00:00:12,021
Without evidence, settlement waits or the business carries more risk.

3
00:00:12,071 --> 00:00:15,736
The operator holds the private ledger and witness.

4
00:00:15,786 --> 00:00:19,450
Sworn creates independently verifiable evidence without exposing transactions.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:25,882
The operator selects the batch in Sworn's local console and starts a proof job.

6
00:00:25,932 --> 00:00:30,936
Sworn runs Tempo's own Zone verification code in a zero-knowledge VM,

7
00:00:30,986 --> 00:00:36,450
then creates proof evidence that a third party can verify on chain.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,058
On Moderato, our own one-operator Zone, not a Tempo-created one,

9
00:00:41,108 --> 00:00:47,970
settles a batch only after Sworn's proof passes; only then can a withdrawal be paid.

10
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:51,195
Three batches, proven and checked on chain.

11
00:00:51,245 --> 00:00:56,264
A forged batch, even signed by our own sequencer, is rejected.

12
00:00:56,314 --> 00:00:59,950
Anchor to payout: fifty-eight minutes, on one laptop.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,488
First buyer: a Zone business whose reviewer cannot reconstruct the private witness.

14
00:01:05,538 --> 00:01:09,642
A signed report or generic proof is not enough:

15
00:01:09,692 --> 00:01:13,335
the reviewer needs evidence of exact Tempo execution.

16
00:01:13,385 --> 00:01:17,950
One batch tests demand; repeats or upgrades become Proof Operations.

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,580
Sworn is Tempo-specific, not generic ZK: it runs Zone code,

18
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:26,283
fits the portal's batch shape, and tracks upgrades.

19
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:30,450
We begin as Proof Operations for a Zone business.

20
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:37,394
Later, Tempo could add this as an independent check alongside its TEE, not replace it.

21
00:01:37,444 --> 00:01:42,950
I work on Reth and Revm, with fifteen years in banking systems.

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,343
Today: testnet, unaudited.

23
00:01:44,393 --> 00:01:45,736
No customer claimed.

24
00:01:45,786 --> 00:01:53,164
Next, a design partner supplies a batch and decides if independent proof is worth paying for.

25
00:01:53,214 --> 00:01:55,950
Sworn: audit-ready evidence for private execution.
